I've implemented the four speedups, plus tests and design notes. They don't take effect yet: `.specdojo/exec-defaults.yaml` is protected, so someone has to apply the proposed config. The 1-stage time hasn't been measured before vs. after, and the post-integration `npm run check` on develop hasn't been run. The sandbox can't launch real runs, so both need a human.

**What changed:**
- **Choosing parent validations by change type:** an entry in `pipeline.parent_validations` can now take `paths` (globs). If no file the executor changed matches, that validation is skipped and recorded as `not_applicable`. That status doesn't count as a failure, and an executor `not_run` for the same check is accepted. Every validation still runs when it has no `paths`, when the change list is missing or truncated, or when re-validating after the integration target was merged in.
- **Integration commit:** the new `pipeline.commit_hook_skips` (`{ hook, covered_by }`) skips a hook via `LEFTHOOK_EXCLUDE` only when all its `covered_by` validations `passed` in that run. A skipped (`not_applicable`) validation does not let its hook be skipped. Manual commits and product-repo commits keep every hook.
- **Reporter:** with `pipeline.mechanical_result: true`, the runner writes a completed edit result itself from the executor's `final_message`, without starting the reporter. Review, blocked results, an empty `final_message` and rendering failures still go to the reporter. A test confirms the result passes the reporter JSON Schema, keeps its frontmatter, and passes markdownlint and the unfilled check.
- **Worktree preparation:** `npm ci` now runs with `--prefer-offline --no-audit --no-fund`. I didn't reuse `specdojo build`: per the code comment it takes seconds, and its output depends on the worktree's files.
- **Design and guides:** `sysd-agent-settings` has a new section, 「1 段の所要時間を減らす処理」. It covers why skipped hooks are safe given the passed evidence, and which result fields the runner writes versus the reporter. The exec config guide, worktree guide and schema are updated too. The ticket's 対応結果 records the decisions, the config proposal, the CHANGELOG items and what's left.

**Checks:** history-link validation and markdownlint on the changed docs passed. As a sanity check I also ran `tsc --noEmit` and the related unit tests (279 passed). The parent runner's typecheck, lint and test results are the official ones.

**Decisions to confirm:**
- In the proposed config, `test-unit` has no `paths`, so it still runs on every change. Unit tests read the real docs (the sidebar kata-menu test, the catalog tests), so it can't safely be skipped for docs. `validate-schema` also runs every time, and `catalog validate` still runs from lefthook at the integration commit.
- Even when the runner writes the result, the pipeline state records the assigned reporter as the actor. Resuming the integration stage uses that actor for register transitions, and `runner` isn't on the roster. The result's 進め方 section says the runner wrote it.
- `mechanical_result` defaults to `false`, so existing users' results aren't silently written by the runner instead.

The ticket input says `parent_validation_concurrency` was set to 2, but the current config has 1 (set back on 2026-11-14 because of load). The proposal keeps 1.

